274
00:16:58,390 --> 00:16:59,400
Fine.

275
00:17:10,050 --> 00:17:12,790
Mr. Thear, Miss Praewa is here
to see you.

276
00:17:15,210 --> 00:17:16,890
Sh*t, she came all the way to my house?

277
00:17:17,340 --> 00:17:18,030
What should I do?

278
00:17:18,820 --> 00:17:19,610
What am I going to do?

279
00:17:19,950 --> 00:17:20,620
What do I do now?

280
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:22,350
In that case, I'll leave now.

281
00:17:22,670 --> 00:17:24,500
You stay here
and have fun with your girl.

282
00:17:25,610 --> 00:17:26,980
Hey, Mungkorn! Wait.

283
00:17:27,410 --> 00:17:28,110
What?

284
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:30,980
You need to help me.

285
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:31,840
Help with what?

286
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:32,970
Please...

287
00:17:33,150 --> 00:17:36,190
pretend to be in love with me
for a bit longer.

288
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:37,700
No way.

289
00:17:38,310 --> 00:17:39,870
If she sees us and finds out,

290
00:17:40,140 --> 00:17:41,240
she'll turn it into a huge deal.

291
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:42,920
- I'm leaving.
- Please, I'm begging you.

292
00:17:42,950 --> 00:17:44,460
So she'll finally leave me alone.

293
00:17:45,380 --> 00:17:46,300
And then...

294
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:49,490
I can focus on you and only you.

295
00:18:15,180 --> 00:18:16,120
What are you doing?

296
00:18:16,860 --> 00:18:17,840
Thear!

297
00:18:19,230 --> 00:18:20,330
What is going on here?

298
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:23,170
Oh, Praewa...
What brings you here?

299
00:18:23,300 --> 00:18:26,050
You said you'd text me after showering,

300
00:18:26,250 --> 00:18:28,350
but it's been a whole week,
and you still haven't replied.

301
00:18:28,380 --> 00:18:29,500
Did it take you that long to shower?

302
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:32,270
Oh...

303
00:18:33,090 --> 00:18:34,190
I was busy getting married.

304
00:18:34,390 --> 00:18:35,030
What?

305
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:37,520
See? This is my love.

306
00:18:42,150 --> 00:18:43,000
What are you doing?

307
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:44,550
Come on, honey.

308
00:18:44,910 --> 00:18:46,280
We're both in the police force.

309
00:18:47,330 --> 00:18:49,530
We understand each other so well,
and we're a great match.

310
00:18:49,570 --> 00:18:52,800
Most importantly, he's so protective
and cares deeply about me.

311
00:18:53,710 --> 00:18:55,690
I wouldn't go that far, honey.

312
00:18:56,710 --> 00:18:58,120
But if anyone tries to mess with him,

313
00:18:59,570 --> 00:19:00,770
I'm not going to let it slide.

314
00:19:13,290 --> 00:19:14,090
Come here, honey.

315
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:16,040
- Yes?
- You've got something on your lip.

316
00:19:16,060 --> 00:19:16,670
Where?

317
00:19:17,300 --> 00:19:18,020
Right...

318
00:19:18,450 --> 00:19:19,180
here!

319
00:19:21,690 --> 00:19:23,550
Wow, you taste so sweet.

320
00:19:26,210 --> 00:19:27,460
I'm sorry, Praewa.

321
00:19:27,940 --> 00:19:30,620
I don't think we can
keep seeing each other anymore.

322
00:19:31,070 --> 00:19:32,070
Please just move on.

323
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:33,770
Oh, wait a second.

324
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:37,190
Don't you dare tell anyone about this.

325
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:39,610
This is classified information.

326
00:19:40,670 --> 00:19:42,670
You always have so many excuses.

327
00:19:42,690 --> 00:19:44,500
My heart is literally breaking.

328
00:19:44,530 --> 00:19:46,690
Why would I tell anyone?
I'm too embarrassed.

329
00:19:46,710 --> 00:19:48,540
- Praewa... Hold on! Come back!
- Don't call my name!

330
00:19:48,570 --> 00:19:49,890
- Praewa!
- Stop calling me!

331
00:19:50,040 --> 00:19:53,710
No!

332
00:19:53,740 --> 00:19:55,450
Bye-bye.

333
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:59,360
Dodged another bullet.

334
00:20:00,010 --> 00:20:01,320
Well done, honey.

335
00:20:02,810 --> 00:20:03,750
Honey?

336
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:08,360
Why don't I feel that way at all?

337
00:20:11,030 --> 00:20:13,940
I feel more like your servant,

338
00:20:14,790 --> 00:20:15,940
your good-luck charm,

339
00:20:17,270 --> 00:20:18,450
and your decoy date.

340
00:20:20,790 --> 00:20:21,790
What do you mean?

341
00:20:22,530 --> 00:20:24,350
What exactly am I to you?

342
00:20:32,820 --> 00:20:33,730
Mungkorn...

343
00:20:45,480 --> 00:20:46,850
Mungkorn, don't be afraid.

344
00:20:47,050 --> 00:20:49,210
Just tell the truth about
what's going on between you and Thear,

345
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:50,660
and everything will be fine.

346
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:52,190
If you don't stop messing with us,

347
00:20:52,220 --> 00:20:53,720
I'll interrogate you, too.

348
00:20:53,750 --> 00:20:55,130
"If you don't stop messing with us,

349
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:57,010
I'll interrogate you, too."

350
00:20:57,150 --> 00:20:59,350
Oh, I'm shaking in my boots, you dork.

351
00:20:59,730 --> 00:21:01,700
Thear and Mungkorn are innocent anyway.

352
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:03,800
- Mungkorn, tell the truth.
- Please leave.

353
00:21:04,050 --> 00:21:04,710
- Go!
- What?

354
00:21:04,730 --> 00:21:05,940
- I have to work.
- Mungkorn!

355
00:21:34,180 --> 00:21:35,520
How would you explain this?

356
00:21:40,030 --> 00:21:40,710
- Sh*t.
- Sh*t.

357
00:21:42,550 --> 00:21:43,880
Mungkorn, are you okay?

358
00:21:43,970 --> 00:21:44,840
I'm fine.

359
00:21:45,470 --> 00:21:47,980
You bastard.
You want me to get rough with you, huh?

360
00:21:53,190 --> 00:21:54,070
Inspector!

361
00:21:54,350 --> 00:21:54,980
Inspector!

362
00:21:59,050 --> 00:21:59,850
Are you alright?

363
00:22:24,120 --> 00:22:25,580
What exactly do you want me to explain?

364
00:22:25,600 --> 00:22:27,600
Are you two spies
for the Black Bull gang?

365
00:22:27,920 --> 00:22:28,570
What?

366
00:22:30,100 --> 00:22:32,280
Did you intentionally silence Ronnaphop?

367
00:22:32,580 --> 00:22:34,400
Hold on, this is getting out of hand.

368
00:22:34,950 --> 00:22:36,500
Did Thear make you do it,

369
00:22:37,050 --> 00:22:38,220
or did you do it of your own free will?

370
00:22:38,450 --> 00:22:40,800
Make me do what?
What are you even talking about?

371
00:22:41,190 --> 00:22:43,400
What is the secret
between the two of you?

372
00:22:44,070 --> 00:22:46,110
There really was nothing.

373
00:22:48,290 --> 00:22:50,150
Giving a false statement is a crime.

374
00:22:51,220 --> 00:22:51,850
Well...

375
00:22:53,360 --> 00:22:53,940
I...

376
00:22:54,030 --> 00:22:55,080
What about right now?

377
00:22:56,080 --> 00:22:57,360
There is still nothing.

378
00:22:58,590 --> 00:22:59,800
Dammit, this piece of junk!

379
00:22:59,870 --> 00:23:00,680
Captain,

380
00:23:00,950 --> 00:23:02,210
I think this thing is broken.

381
00:23:02,230 --> 00:23:03,720
This machine only tells the truth.

382
00:23:05,090 --> 00:23:06,430
What is the secret

383
00:23:06,660 --> 00:23:07,590
between the two of you?

384
00:23:09,180 --> 00:23:10,480
Whatever it is, just come clean.

385
00:23:14,300 --> 00:23:15,100
Ugh!

386
00:23:15,740 --> 00:23:17,000
I don't really know myself.

387
00:23:18,690 --> 00:23:20,520
He just comes and goes as he pleases.

388
00:23:21,710 --> 00:23:23,690
He's probably just
playing with my feelings.

389
00:23:31,890 --> 00:23:32,530
Wait...

390
00:23:34,930 --> 00:23:37,710
Are you two in a relationship?

391
00:23:39,230 --> 00:23:40,090
No, we're not.

392
00:23:44,560 --> 00:23:46,150
We're just married.

393
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:47,190
Married?

394
00:23:48,230 --> 00:23:49,700
It was a marriage
to turn his luck around.

395
00:23:51,850 --> 00:23:52,980
Now we're just waiting
for the day we split up.

396
00:24:17,120 --> 00:24:18,330
Don't worry.

397
00:24:18,860 --> 00:24:19,860
I won't tell anyone.

398
00:24:22,300 --> 00:24:23,620
Thank you, Captain.

399
00:24:24,760 --> 00:24:26,810
I don't want to have any trouble
with the inspector either.

400
00:24:30,650 --> 00:24:33,870
But if you ever need to talk,
you can talk to me.

401
00:24:35,490 --> 00:24:36,450
Please feel free.

402
00:24:39,610 --> 00:24:40,250
Thank you.

403
00:24:49,020 --> 00:24:50,780
Oh, Mungkorn?

404
00:24:51,440 --> 00:24:53,000
Why are you home so early today?

405
00:24:53,720 --> 00:24:56,560
They sent me home
while the case is under review.

406
00:24:57,230 --> 00:24:59,580
What's with the sad face?

407
00:25:00,070 --> 00:25:01,200
Come talk to me, dear.

408
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:08,790
What happened?

409
00:25:09,030 --> 00:25:11,530
Lately, things seem strange
between you and Thear.

410
00:25:13,290 --> 00:25:15,390
Did you guys fail to become one?

411
00:25:17,570 --> 00:25:19,050
It has nothing to do with that.

412
00:25:19,410 --> 00:25:20,830
Nothing at all.

413
00:25:21,710 --> 00:25:23,550
Then what is it, dear?

414
00:25:24,150 --> 00:25:26,050
Or is it that Thear
isn't taking good care of you?

415
00:25:26,990 --> 00:25:28,460
If he's done anything wrong,

416
00:25:28,510 --> 00:25:30,720
you can tell me.
I'll deal with him for you.

417
00:25:31,290 --> 00:25:32,760
Or are there women bothering you?

418
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:39,690
I'm just lonely.

419
00:25:43,450 --> 00:25:44,970
Ever since I moved here,

420
00:25:46,990 --> 00:25:49,840
I've felt like I don't quite belong.

421
00:25:55,680 --> 00:25:59,070
But it's probably nothing.
I think I'm just homesick.

422
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:03,400
See? He really isn't
taking care of you well enough.

423
00:26:04,040 --> 00:26:06,900
If you want to go home,
then you should be allowed to go.

424
00:26:07,900 --> 00:26:09,980
Thear, come here.

425
00:26:16,700 --> 00:26:18,260
How did you know I was eavesdropping?

426
00:26:18,770 --> 00:26:20,400
Mother knows best, you know?

427
00:26:21,890 --> 00:26:24,150
You always do this
when you've done something wrong.

428
00:26:24,700 --> 00:26:25,990
What? I haven't done anything wrong.

429
00:26:26,020 --> 00:26:26,950
Stop talking back.

430
00:26:28,090 --> 00:26:31,370
Since you're free right now,
take Mungkorn back home for a visit.

431
00:26:32,250 --> 00:26:35,130
Mom, with my luck this bad,
you want me to drive?

432
00:26:35,470 --> 00:26:36,850
I'll end up in a fatal crash. No way.

433
00:26:37,250 --> 00:26:37,960
Wait,

434
00:26:38,630 --> 00:26:39,850
you've already become one.

435
00:26:40,150 --> 00:26:41,510
How would you still have bad luck?

436
00:26:42,870 --> 00:26:44,880
Become one?

437
00:26:46,590 --> 00:26:47,780
Oh, right.

438
00:26:47,860 --> 00:26:49,900
We have become one, haven't we?

439
00:26:50,320 --> 00:26:52,220
I totally forgot. I was wrong.

440
00:26:52,390 --> 00:26:53,630
Yes, we've done it.

441
00:26:54,730 --> 00:26:55,730
Then that's settled.

442
00:26:56,390 --> 00:26:57,980
Take him back home for a visit.

443
00:26:58,680 --> 00:27:01,670
If there's any misunderstanding,
talk it out.

444
00:27:02,400 --> 00:27:05,360
If you've done anything wrong,
apologize to him.

445
00:27:05,720 --> 00:27:07,190
Do you understand what I'm saying?

446
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:11,930
Aren't you taking this a little too far?

447
00:27:12,230 --> 00:27:14,070
It's like you love him more than me now.

448
00:27:15,090 --> 00:27:15,780
I can't help it.

449
00:27:16,140 --> 00:27:17,710
He's just so adorable.

450
00:27:37,200 --> 00:27:44,520
(Phayao)

451
00:27:58,050 --> 00:28:00,310
I told you
not to wear the ring outside,

452
00:28:00,550 --> 00:28:01,540
and you took it that seriously, huh?

453
00:28:02,210 --> 00:28:03,500
It's a direct order from my boss.

454
00:28:04,510 --> 00:28:05,540
I have to follow it.

455
00:28:07,490 --> 00:28:09,620
I never thought of you
as just a placeholder

456
00:28:09,640 --> 00:28:10,980
or my decoy date.

457
00:28:12,160 --> 00:28:14,220
The reason I'm always
ordering you around

458
00:28:14,660 --> 00:28:16,160
is simply because I enjoy teasing you.

459
00:28:16,730 --> 00:28:18,790
You're actually pretty cute
when you're annoyed.

460
00:28:20,950 --> 00:28:22,420
But I know now that
you don't like it.

461
00:28:22,540 --> 00:28:23,380
I'm sorry for that.

462
00:28:24,490 --> 00:28:27,010
When I told Praewa
that you're my husband,

463
00:28:27,530 --> 00:28:28,780
I just wanted to show you
the respect you deserve.

464
00:28:33,930 --> 00:28:35,350
I'll try my best to believe that.

465
00:28:36,610 --> 00:28:38,550
If you don't believe me,
look at this. Hang on.

466
00:28:40,160 --> 00:28:40,710
Here.

467
00:28:41,130 --> 00:28:43,540
I've texted every girl in my contacts

468
00:28:44,160 --> 00:28:45,170
to tell them I'm already married.

469
00:28:45,410 --> 00:28:46,300
See for yourself.

470
00:28:47,140 --> 00:28:48,500
I'm not going to do that.

471
00:28:49,300 --> 00:28:50,200
Just put it away.

472
00:28:54,270 --> 00:28:54,940
Listen.

473
00:28:55,510 --> 00:28:58,430
I just want you to know that
if I'm ever serious about someone,

474
00:28:58,510 --> 00:29:00,380
I'll be completely faithful
and love them with all my heart.

475
00:29:00,960 --> 00:29:03,520
I'll always respect the person I love.

476
00:29:05,820 --> 00:29:06,890
Come on, Inspector.

477
00:29:07,600 --> 00:29:09,520
You don't need to explain this to me.

478
00:29:10,740 --> 00:29:13,510
It doesn't really matter to me anyway

479
00:29:14,010 --> 00:29:17,460
because I'm not the one you love
in the first place.

480
00:29:18,250 --> 00:29:19,290
Well, just in case.

481
00:29:19,990 --> 00:29:21,870
We never know what the future holds.

482
00:29:22,450 --> 00:29:24,330
If you happen to fall in love with me,

483
00:29:24,610 --> 00:29:25,860
at least you'll know

484
00:29:26,240 --> 00:29:27,270
that I make a great lover.

485
00:29:30,770 --> 00:29:32,640
And about that time you asked

486
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:34,840
if I had to use a lot of imagination,

487
00:29:36,370 --> 00:29:38,750
do you want to know
what was actually on my mind?

488
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:43,030
You were probably thinking
of someone you actually like.

489
00:29:44,710 --> 00:29:47,170
I was thinking about
how nice it would be

490
00:29:47,590 --> 00:29:49,100
if we could actually do it together

491
00:29:49,990 --> 00:29:52,950
because we both wanted to,
not just to fix my luck.

492
00:29:53,490 --> 00:29:55,210
♪Trying...♪

493
00:30:03,280 --> 00:30:08,160
♪Let me remind you
what our deal was all about,♪

494
00:30:08,180 --> 00:30:13,050
♪No falling in love,
no feelings allowed♪

495
00:30:13,080 --> 00:30:17,960
♪I'm just a name on your contract,
you're just passing through,♪

496
00:30:17,990 --> 00:30:22,840
♪So stay on your side,
and I'll stay on mine, too♪

497
00:30:25,300 --> 00:30:26,000
Mom!

498
00:30:26,390 --> 00:30:27,920
I'm home.

499
00:30:29,270 --> 00:30:31,270
- Missed you so much.
- I missed you so much, sweetie.

500
00:30:31,300 --> 00:30:32,120
Let me give you a kiss.

501
00:30:33,500 --> 00:30:34,060
One more.

502
00:30:34,590 --> 00:30:36,290
That's enough! Thear is watching.

503
00:30:36,590 --> 00:30:38,110
One more right here.

504
00:30:38,350 --> 00:30:39,820
Know your place, Inspector.

505
00:30:41,130 --> 00:30:42,370
What's going on?

506
00:30:42,390 --> 00:30:45,100
We just met at the wedding.

507
00:30:45,360 --> 00:30:46,710
Why the rush to come back and see me?

508
00:30:46,740 --> 00:30:48,510
Well, I missed you.

509
00:30:48,560 --> 00:30:49,640
I was worried about you, too,

510
00:30:49,960 --> 00:30:51,210
so he drove me here.

511
00:30:51,650 --> 00:30:52,570
Hello, Mom.

512
00:30:52,820 --> 00:30:53,830
Hello, dear.

513
00:30:54,020 --> 00:30:54,830
Inspector,

514
00:30:54,900 --> 00:30:57,210
- you shouldn't spoil him so much.
- Hey!

515
00:30:57,810 --> 00:30:58,770
It's alright, Mom.

516
00:30:58,800 --> 00:31:00,770
I've wanted to visit his home
for a while now.

517
00:31:01,750 --> 00:31:03,680
Oh, you've come at the perfect time.

518
00:31:03,850 --> 00:31:06,500
The temple here is holding a fair.

519
00:31:06,770 --> 00:31:08,870
Why don't you take him there?

520
00:31:09,950 --> 00:31:13,080
Mom, it's a temple fair,
not a pub or a bar.

521
00:31:13,760 --> 00:31:15,230
He wouldn't know how to have fun
at a place like that.

522
00:31:15,280 --> 00:31:17,460
Come on, I'm a simple guy.

523
00:31:17,480 --> 00:31:18,860
I'm not that fancy.

524
00:31:18,980 --> 00:31:19,900
I know how to enjoy a fair.

525
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:22,610
Let's take your things upstairs

526
00:31:22,640 --> 00:31:24,490
and check out your bedroom.

527
00:31:24,750 --> 00:31:27,500
I'm going to cook
some delicious food for you.

528
00:31:28,360 --> 00:31:29,640
Make me lots of food, Mom!

529
00:31:29,660 --> 00:31:31,740
I've missed your cooking so much.

530
00:31:32,080 --> 00:31:33,040
Alright, sweetie.

531
00:31:33,120 --> 00:31:34,340
You'd better eat a lot, okay?

532
00:31:38,300 --> 00:31:39,520
Alright, I'll go grab the bags.

533
00:31:44,190 --> 00:31:46,650
Hey there, Hunglay!

534
00:31:48,370 --> 00:31:49,360
How have you been, buddy?

535
00:31:53,500 --> 00:31:54,730
Khao Jao!

536
00:31:54,850 --> 00:31:55,860
My boy!

537
00:31:56,400 --> 00:31:57,720
It's been so long.

538
00:31:58,060 --> 00:31:59,110
I miss you so much!

539
00:31:59,590 --> 00:32:00,490
Daddy misses you.

540
00:32:00,740 --> 00:32:02,150
Look how much you've grown.

541
00:32:02,970 --> 00:32:04,270
I missed you so much.

542
00:32:05,010 --> 00:32:06,980
Is this your cat? He's cute.

543
00:32:07,500 --> 00:32:08,200
Yes.

544
00:32:08,270 --> 00:32:09,820
He was a stray.

545
00:32:10,010 --> 00:32:12,390
But after a while,
he basically became my son.

546
00:32:13,550 --> 00:32:15,040
What was his name again? Khao Jao?

547
00:32:15,870 --> 00:32:17,520
- Can you salute for me?
- Hello, sir!

548
00:32:17,690 --> 00:32:18,870
Hello. Salute!

549
00:32:21,400 --> 00:32:22,300
Oh, Inspector.

550
00:32:22,470 --> 00:32:24,310
Please pass me that VIF Jelly.

551
00:32:24,650 --> 00:32:26,070
That red pouch right there.

552
00:32:26,350 --> 00:32:27,450
- This one?
- Yes.

553
00:32:29,200 --> 00:32:30,320
Want me to tear it open?

554
00:32:30,380 --> 00:32:31,180
Yes, please.

555
00:32:32,800 --> 00:32:33,960
Come here.

556
00:32:39,660 --> 00:32:40,460
Thank you.

557
00:32:41,610 --> 00:32:42,500
Come here.

558
00:32:47,830 --> 00:32:48,960
Now I know...

559
00:32:49,650 --> 00:32:51,540
why you always have cat food with you.

560
00:32:53,840 --> 00:32:54,870
You're just like a cat.

561
00:32:55,550 --> 00:32:56,990
That's why you attract them.

562
00:32:59,500 --> 00:33:00,850
Wanna try this? Meow!

563
00:33:01,400 --> 00:33:02,700
Wanna try? I'll open it for you.

564
00:33:03,530 --> 00:33:04,850
Just feed Khao Jao.

565
00:33:08,870 --> 00:33:09,740
Khao Jao...

566
00:33:09,760 --> 00:33:11,020
Have you been getting any treats?

567
00:33:32,200 --> 00:33:33,530
The house is a bit old.

568
00:33:34,700 --> 00:33:35,930
Come to think about it,

569
00:33:36,530 --> 00:33:39,120
my whole house is smaller
than your kitchen.

570
00:33:40,080 --> 00:33:41,550
Why are you comparing them?

571
00:33:41,580 --> 00:33:43,710
I think it's quite cozy.

572
00:33:44,790 --> 00:33:46,160
It is cozy,

573
00:33:46,980 --> 00:33:48,740
but I've always wanted a big house

574
00:33:48,830 --> 00:33:50,510
to give my mom
a safe, comfortable home.

575
00:33:52,250 --> 00:33:54,760
Well, you'll be getting
your marriage money soon.

576
00:33:55,290 --> 00:33:57,800
You can get her a new house.
I'll be the one footing the bill.

577
00:34:00,790 --> 00:34:02,270
Come on, let me help you unpack.

578
00:34:03,800 --> 00:34:04,780
Let me put this here.

579
00:34:18,180 --> 00:34:20,090
(Pol.Snr.Sgt.Maj. Worawit Phianwanich,
Deceased January 27, 2005)

580
00:34:20,110 --> 00:34:21,520
Is this your dad, Mungkorn?

581
00:34:31,580 --> 00:34:32,210
Yes.

582
00:34:35,410 --> 00:34:37,190
My dad was a police officer, too.

583
00:34:37,220 --> 00:34:39,580
(Pol.Snr.Sgt.Maj. Worawit Phianwanich,
Deceased January 27, 2005)

584
00:34:40,140 --> 00:34:41,540
How did he pass away?

585
00:34:42,670 --> 00:34:44,240
He was shot.

586
00:34:45,970 --> 00:34:47,860
He was an incredibly honest officer,

587
00:34:49,400 --> 00:34:51,010
and that made him a target
for a lot of people.

588
00:34:51,030 --> 00:34:52,780
(Pol.Snr.Sgt.Maj. Worawit Phianwanich,
Deceased January 27, 2005)

589
00:34:53,070 --> 00:34:54,340
It's because of him...

590
00:34:55,830 --> 00:34:57,360
that I want to be a good cop.

591
00:34:59,450 --> 00:35:01,330
I want to follow in his footsteps
and make him proud,

592
00:35:03,510 --> 00:35:04,890
but my mom tried to stop me.

593
00:35:06,890 --> 00:35:08,430
She's afraid I'll end up just like him.

594
00:35:11,060 --> 00:35:13,050
You're a good cop, though.

595
00:35:14,670 --> 00:35:17,210
I'm sure your dad
would be so proud of you.

596
00:35:20,390 --> 00:35:22,050
Wait, you play the guitar, too?

597
00:35:25,040 --> 00:35:25,750
Yeah.

598
00:35:26,310 --> 00:35:27,980
If I weren't a cop,

599
00:35:28,550 --> 00:35:30,760
I'd probably be a musician by now.

600
00:35:32,180 --> 00:35:33,730
Play something for me, then.

601
00:35:34,580 --> 00:35:36,370
The thing is, I'm not in the mood.

602
00:35:36,670 --> 00:35:38,540
I only play when the mood strikes.

603
00:35:39,570 --> 00:35:40,530
Oh, really?

604
00:35:41,380 --> 00:35:42,800
You have to wait for the mood, huh?

605
00:35:44,290 --> 00:35:45,280
Alright, then.

606
00:35:48,110 --> 00:35:49,750
Then I'll get you in the mood myself.

607
00:35:51,250 --> 00:35:52,600
What should I do?

608
00:35:57,180 --> 00:35:58,250
Does this get you in the mood?

609
00:36:13,320 --> 00:36:14,170
What are you doing?

610
00:36:17,090 --> 00:36:18,420
Can you sleep like this...

611
00:36:18,930 --> 00:36:20,220
on a floor mattress
under a mosquito net?

612
00:36:21,470 --> 00:36:23,210
I'll let you sleep by yourself tonight.

613
00:36:23,310 --> 00:36:24,540
I'll sleep in my mom's room.

614
00:36:25,310 --> 00:36:26,560
No way.

615
00:36:26,840 --> 00:36:28,040
You have to sleep with me.

616
00:36:28,380 --> 00:36:29,860
I'm too scared to sleep alone.

617
00:36:29,960 --> 00:36:31,090
I'm not used to this place.

618
00:36:33,690 --> 00:36:34,630
And...

619
00:36:35,240 --> 00:36:37,820
I need some warmth from you.

620
00:37:21,710 --> 00:37:22,600
Nothing moved.

621
00:37:25,620 --> 00:37:27,050
Back before the police exam,

622
00:37:27,070 --> 00:37:28,700
I used to practice with an airsoft gun,

623
00:37:28,720 --> 00:37:30,700
using these tin cans as targets.

624
00:37:31,810 --> 00:37:33,710
But no matter how much I practiced,
I could never hit them.

625
00:37:34,520 --> 00:37:35,800
I'm not as good as you.

626
00:37:37,420 --> 00:37:40,300
Well, nobody needs
to be good at everything,

627
00:37:41,040 --> 00:37:45,020
but I think everyone has
at least one thing they're good at.

628
00:37:49,350 --> 00:37:51,220
What would you say you're good at, then?

629
00:37:53,420 --> 00:37:55,830
I think I'm good at...

630
00:38:11,860 --> 00:38:14,340
I'm good at making people fall for me.

631
00:38:14,840 --> 00:38:16,730
Anyone who gets close to me
ends up falling for me.

632
00:38:17,120 --> 00:38:19,140
I never miss a target I set my sight on.

633
00:38:43,880 --> 00:38:45,710
Who exactly told you that?

634
00:38:46,300 --> 00:38:47,940
Got some kind of certification
to prove it?

635
00:38:48,940 --> 00:38:50,340
I don't need anyone to tell me.

636
00:38:51,320 --> 00:38:54,160
I can see it for myself,
and I can feel it.

637
00:38:56,090 --> 00:38:57,840
I think the only thing
you're truly an expert at

638
00:38:58,780 --> 00:39:00,890
is imagining things.

639
00:39:36,150 --> 00:39:37,750
You don't have to
wrap your arms around me.

640
00:39:39,310 --> 00:39:41,630
I don't think I'm just imagining things.

641
00:40:01,650 --> 00:40:03,140
Time to eat, guys.

642
00:40:03,630 --> 00:40:05,190
Dinner's ready.

643
00:40:07,130 --> 00:40:07,770
Coming, Mom.

644
00:40:07,820 --> 00:40:08,450
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

645
00:40:10,820 --> 00:40:11,480
Hey.

646
00:40:22,900 --> 00:40:25,070
Here, try some nam prik num.

647
00:40:25,680 --> 00:40:26,450
Thank you.

648
00:40:26,610 --> 00:40:28,920
You have to try this one, though,

649
00:40:28,940 --> 00:40:31,120
because it's Mungkorn's favorite.

650
00:40:31,250 --> 00:40:32,420
It's called ab ong-or.

651
00:40:33,540 --> 00:40:35,110
What was it again? Ab...

652
00:40:35,310 --> 00:40:37,610
- Ab ong-or.
- Ab ong-or...

653
00:40:37,740 --> 00:40:38,980
- Right.
- Whoa, that's new.

654
00:40:40,070 --> 00:40:40,820
Let me see.

655
00:40:48,550 --> 00:40:49,760
This is delicious.

656
00:40:50,440 --> 00:40:51,370
I haven't had Northern food

657
00:40:51,400 --> 00:40:53,750
this authentic in a long time.

658
00:40:55,290 --> 00:40:56,100
What?

659
00:40:56,390 --> 00:40:58,460
You're from the North,
but you barely eat Northern food?

660
00:41:00,820 --> 00:41:02,270
That's just how I am.

661
00:41:02,600 --> 00:41:05,090
I never realize how good
the things right in front of me are

662
00:41:06,150 --> 00:41:08,130
until I try them and get hooked.

663
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:14,170
Mungkorn knows
how to cook Northern food, too.

664
00:41:14,440 --> 00:41:16,890
You should cook for him sometime.

665
00:41:17,190 --> 00:41:19,220
You've got some cooking skills
of your own.

666
00:41:19,580 --> 00:41:20,650
That's true.

667
00:41:20,920 --> 00:41:22,650
If Mungkorn were to cook for me,

668
00:41:22,670 --> 00:41:25,060
I'd rush home to eat every single day.

669
00:41:25,320 --> 00:41:27,770
Mom, don't listen to him too much.

670
00:41:27,890 --> 00:41:30,090
At his place, he has people
cook for him every day.

671
00:41:30,120 --> 00:41:31,390
No, no.

672
00:41:31,650 --> 00:41:35,120
Regardless, you still have to cook
for your husband once in a while.

673
00:41:36,140 --> 00:41:37,700
I couldn't agree more.

674
00:41:37,940 --> 00:41:39,280
You can't skip out on that.

675
00:41:39,310 --> 00:41:41,570
You have to cook for your husband
every now and then.

676
00:41:42,400 --> 00:41:44,130
Here, have some nam prik ong.

677
00:41:44,270 --> 00:41:44,830
Here.

678
00:41:45,350 --> 00:41:47,530
- Thank you.
- Eat it with some pork cracklings.

679
00:41:47,550 --> 00:41:49,250
Here, eat some pork cracklings, too.

680
00:41:50,160 --> 00:41:52,400
Can you feed me the pork cracklings?

681
00:41:55,040 --> 00:41:56,060
Your hands work just fine, don't they?

682
00:41:56,080 --> 00:41:58,540
Come on, you've got to take care of me.

683
00:41:59,410 --> 00:42:00,250
Look at him, Mom.

684
00:42:13,800 --> 00:42:15,150
It's so good, Mom.

685
00:42:15,580 --> 00:42:17,630
Seriously delicious. So yummy!

686
00:42:17,650 --> 00:42:19,080
I fried it myself.

687
00:42:29,760 --> 00:42:31,760
Are you sure this thing still runs?

688
00:42:32,260 --> 00:42:33,240
It does.

689
00:42:33,570 --> 00:42:36,150
It just takes a bit of work
to start the engine

690
00:42:36,670 --> 00:42:37,870
since I haven't ridden it in ages.

691
00:42:41,680 --> 00:42:42,510
I think

692
00:42:42,810 --> 00:42:44,730
you should get a new one.
This is too old. It's not gonna make it.

693
00:42:44,900 --> 00:42:46,290
No, it's a waste of money.

694
00:42:46,950 --> 00:42:49,760
Plus, I really love this bike.

695
00:42:50,150 --> 00:42:52,150
It means a lot to me.

696
00:42:54,230 --> 00:42:55,030
Why's that?

697
00:42:56,500 --> 00:42:58,400
I saved up my own money to buy this.

698
00:43:00,220 --> 00:43:01,980
I'm planning to take it
to Chiang Mai with me, too.

699
00:43:09,360 --> 00:43:11,970
- Whoa, alright.
- Good job, Hunglay.

700
00:43:12,530 --> 00:43:14,270
See? Ready to hit the road.

701
00:43:15,800 --> 00:43:17,800
I hope it doesn't break down halfway.

702
00:43:18,680 --> 00:43:19,540
No way.

703
00:43:19,860 --> 00:43:21,830
This old guy can handle anything.

704
00:43:23,120 --> 00:43:24,520
Trust me, Inspector.

705
00:43:25,290 --> 00:43:26,000
Come on.

706
00:43:27,270 --> 00:43:27,900
Okay.

707
00:43:28,550 --> 00:43:30,030
If Hunglay is ready, then let's go.

708
00:43:30,670 --> 00:43:31,810
Are you ready, though?

709
00:43:33,770 --> 00:43:35,410
Alright, let's go, Hunglay!

710
00:43:44,410 --> 00:43:45,070
Is it actually working?

711
00:43:45,100 --> 00:43:47,320
Yeah, it just
hasn't been started in a while.

712
00:43:47,350 --> 00:43:48,370
I haven't started it in a while.

713
00:43:50,110 --> 00:43:51,110
Alright, let's go!

714
00:43:51,370 --> 00:43:52,240
Move it.

715
00:44:31,860 --> 00:44:33,110
Wow, perfect timing.

716
00:44:33,740 --> 00:44:35,350
They're performing
the Sabat Chai drums right now.

717
00:44:35,550 --> 00:44:36,570
Let's go check it out.

718
00:44:36,710 --> 00:44:37,360
Let's go.

719
00:44:50,930 --> 00:44:52,050
My bad.

720
00:44:52,810 --> 00:44:55,880
I got a bit overexcited.
I haven't seen this in a while.

721
00:44:57,610 --> 00:44:59,560
You can keep holding my hand
if you want. I don't mind.

722
00:45:01,090 --> 00:45:02,750
Let's just watch the drum performance.

723
00:45:12,500 --> 00:45:15,460
Is there anyone interested
in trying the Sabat Chai drums?

724
00:45:16,980 --> 00:45:18,260
Why don't you give it a shot?

725
00:45:19,150 --> 00:45:20,780
Me? I don't even know how to play.

726
00:45:22,020 --> 00:45:23,400
Just give it a try.

727
00:45:23,680 --> 00:45:25,640
You're standing here
with your eyes sparkling like that.

728
00:45:26,100 --> 00:45:27,360
I'm sure you can do it.

729
00:45:27,670 --> 00:45:29,130
I'll be right here cheering you on.

730
00:45:29,520 --> 00:45:30,880
I'd rather not, Inspector.

731
00:45:32,000 --> 00:45:34,900
Is there anyone interested
in trying the Sabat Chai drums?

732
00:45:38,400 --> 00:45:40,920
Is there anyone interested
in trying the Sabat Chai drums?

733
00:45:40,940 --> 00:45:41,670
This guy right here!

734
00:45:41,690 --> 00:45:42,850
- Hey, Inspector!
- Please, come on up.

735
00:45:43,490 --> 00:45:44,440
This guy wants to try it!

736
00:45:44,680 --> 00:45:45,680
No!

737
00:45:49,130 --> 00:45:50,110
Let's go.

738
00:45:59,130 --> 00:45:59,880
How do I do it?

739
00:46:03,070 --> 00:46:04,210
Just like this.

740
00:46:40,430 --> 00:46:41,660
Well done!

741
00:46:52,370 --> 00:46:53,170
What's up with you?

742
00:46:53,440 --> 00:46:54,950
You've been smiling the whole time.

743
00:46:55,720 --> 00:46:59,370
I didn't know
you could play the drums that well.

744
00:47:00,100 --> 00:47:01,300
I was just winging it.

745
00:47:01,890 --> 00:47:03,790
Right now, let's forget
about the drum beats.

746
00:47:04,320 --> 00:47:06,090
I'd rather beat someone.

747
00:47:07,450 --> 00:47:09,280
I just wanted you
to be a bit more confident.

748
00:47:10,170 --> 00:47:10,740
Anyway,

749
00:47:11,280 --> 00:47:13,330
I'm so proud of my husband.

750
00:47:24,550 --> 00:47:25,980
What are you looking at?
The teddy bear?

751
00:47:26,840 --> 00:47:28,380
Yeah, it's so cute.

752
00:47:28,660 --> 00:47:31,370
A teddy bear in a police uniform.

753
00:47:33,230 --> 00:47:35,430
That looks just like you.

754
00:47:36,510 --> 00:47:37,790
Want it? I'll win it for you.

755
00:47:38,200 --> 00:47:40,610
It's not as easy as firing a real gun.

756
00:47:41,380 --> 00:47:43,100
They won't give these away easily,

757
00:47:43,490 --> 00:47:45,000
or they'd go out of business.

758
00:47:46,850 --> 00:47:48,310
But if there's anything you want,

759
00:47:48,950 --> 00:47:50,080
I'll get it for you.

760
00:47:54,940 --> 00:47:56,370
- Excuse me, beautiful.
- Yes?

761
00:47:56,370 --> 00:47:58,490
What do I do to get that teddy bear?

762
00:47:58,530 --> 00:48:00,630
Oh, it's just a hundred baht.

763
00:48:00,760 --> 00:48:04,050
You get five bullets,

764
00:48:05,010 --> 00:48:07,610
and every single shot
has to hit the target.

765
00:48:09,090 --> 00:48:10,060
I told you.

766
00:48:10,680 --> 00:48:12,660
This is not as easy
as shooting a real gun.

767
00:48:15,970 --> 00:48:17,650
Then we'll just keep playing
until we win.

768
00:48:20,170 --> 00:48:21,650
Here's a hundred, beautiful.

769
00:48:21,670 --> 00:48:22,920
Thank you.

770
00:48:24,100 --> 00:48:25,100
Since you're talking such a big game,

771
00:48:25,500 --> 00:48:26,740
I challenge you...

772
00:48:26,990 --> 00:48:28,870
to win it in just one try.

773
00:48:32,020 --> 00:48:33,060
Challenge accepted.

774
00:48:45,100 --> 00:48:46,290
We're only getting started.

775
00:48:47,080 --> 00:48:48,060
Was that just pure luck?

776
00:48:54,560 --> 00:48:55,860
Perfect aim.

777
00:48:56,300 --> 00:48:57,310
It's pure luck.

778
00:49:03,370 --> 00:49:05,370
Even John Wick would praise me.

779
00:49:06,580 --> 00:49:07,960
More like John Wack.

780
00:49:14,270 --> 00:49:15,140
I told you.

781
00:49:15,520 --> 00:49:17,060
If there's anything you want,

782
00:49:17,270 --> 00:49:18,440
I'll find a way to get it for you.

783
00:49:19,820 --> 00:49:21,340
Don't get too cocky just yet.

784
00:49:21,790 --> 00:49:23,810
You're definitely going to
miss this one.

785
00:49:41,830 --> 00:49:42,550
See?

786
00:49:43,130 --> 00:49:45,300
I don't back down
from a challenge, you know.

787
00:49:45,330 --> 00:49:47,320
Once I'm challenged, I can do anything.

788
00:49:50,190 --> 00:49:51,350
Yeah, yeah, whatever.

789
00:49:52,820 --> 00:49:53,620
Thank you.

790
00:49:54,810 --> 00:49:56,670
Do you want any more stuffed animals?

791
00:49:57,440 --> 00:49:58,590
Should I win some more for you?

792
00:49:59,410 --> 00:50:01,710
I could do this all night.

793
00:50:02,470 --> 00:50:03,380
No.

794
00:50:03,840 --> 00:50:06,450
Just this police teddy bear is enough.

795
00:50:23,820 --> 00:50:26,220
Now that you've got the bear,
I guess you don't care about me anymore.

796
00:50:29,170 --> 00:50:30,360
Well, it is just too cute.

797
00:50:30,760 --> 00:50:32,050
It looks so cuddly, too.

798
00:50:34,490 --> 00:50:35,750
You think that bear is cuddly?

799
00:50:37,650 --> 00:50:39,230
I'm much more cuddly, though.

800
00:50:46,330 --> 00:50:47,760
Let's go cuddle on the Ferris wheel.

801
00:50:51,560 --> 00:50:52,470
Two people, please.

802
00:50:53,750 --> 00:50:55,130
- Go on, get in.
- Does this go up high?

803
00:51:46,450 --> 00:51:48,350
You can head to bed first.

804
00:51:48,670 --> 00:51:51,120
I think I'll go sit in the gazebo
by the pond for a bit.

805
00:51:51,540 --> 00:51:53,360
It's been a while
since I got to experience this.

806
00:51:55,040 --> 00:51:56,050
I'm not sleepy yet.

807
00:51:56,200 --> 00:51:57,290
Can I come with you?

808
00:51:57,970 --> 00:51:59,180
There are a lot of mosquitoes, though.

809
00:52:00,720 --> 00:52:01,930
I can't go to sleep, then.

810
00:52:02,300 --> 00:52:04,500
I have to stay and make sure
the mosquitoes don't get you.

811
00:52:19,820 --> 00:52:21,920
It's fine. I can apply it myself.

812
00:52:24,060 --> 00:52:25,810
Just keep playing your guitar.
I'll do it for you.

813
00:52:27,140 --> 00:52:27,890
That arm, too.

814
00:52:36,980 --> 00:52:37,680
Okay.

815
00:52:40,300 --> 00:52:41,620
I haven't played this in a while,

816
00:52:42,000 --> 00:52:44,070
so I need to brush up on it a bit.

817
00:52:52,390 --> 00:52:53,550
Try flirting with me using your guitar.

818
00:52:55,890 --> 00:52:57,090
Do I still need to do that?

819
00:52:57,290 --> 00:52:58,830
I'm already married
and living in your house.

820
00:52:59,830 --> 00:53:01,120
Of course you do.

821
00:53:01,380 --> 00:53:03,450
I don't fall for people that easily,
you know.

822
00:53:04,430 --> 00:53:07,310
You've got to show me some moves
before you can win my heart.

823
00:53:08,100 --> 00:53:10,180
I'm not exactly the smooth type.

824
00:53:10,700 --> 00:53:12,860
I'm pretty straightforward
and easy to read.

825
00:53:13,270 --> 00:53:14,900
I'm not very good
at hiding my feelings.

826
00:53:24,360 --> 00:53:25,890
Trust me, I know.

827
00:53:44,460 --> 00:53:49,750
♪I have a heart to give,
When will you receive it?♪

828
00:53:49,920 --> 00:53:54,820
♪Can you hear it?
My love, can you hear my wishes?♪

829
00:53:55,150 --> 00:54:00,500
♪All of my heart, I've kept it all for you,♪

830
00:54:00,730 --> 00:54:05,640
♪And all I want is for it to belong to you♪

831
00:54:08,310 --> 00:54:13,440
♪If you ask how much I love you,
I'll let you know♪

832
00:54:13,650 --> 00:54:18,490
♪If you ask how much I care,
I'll tell you so♪

833
00:54:18,910 --> 00:54:23,800
♪I love you to the moon and back♪

834
00:54:24,170 --> 00:54:29,000
♪That's how much love I have packed♪

835
00:54:29,380 --> 00:54:34,290
♪About four hundred thousand miles,
or even more than that♪

836
00:54:43,280 --> 00:54:44,180
You're really good.

837
00:54:46,470 --> 00:54:48,150
Does this count as you flirting with me?

838
00:54:48,700 --> 00:54:50,430
That song was so romantic.

839
00:54:51,610 --> 00:54:53,610
Think whatever you want.

840
00:54:53,920 --> 00:54:55,730
It's just one of my favorite songs.

841
00:54:56,290 --> 00:54:58,510
It doesn't mean anything
about how I feel.

842
00:55:01,910 --> 00:55:03,930
I wonder if there really is...

843
00:55:03,950 --> 00:55:06,350
someone who could love you
as much as the person in that song does.

844
00:55:06,790 --> 00:55:07,590
I'd really like to know.

845
00:55:09,710 --> 00:55:11,280
I honestly don't know.

846
00:55:12,890 --> 00:55:15,040
I've never loved anyone
that much, either.

847
00:55:19,470 --> 00:55:21,000
Alright, whatever.

848
00:55:21,410 --> 00:55:23,410
I'm going to take
that song you just played

849
00:55:23,690 --> 00:55:26,170
as our love confession.

850
00:55:51,830 --> 00:55:52,390
Ouch!

851
00:55:53,290 --> 00:55:54,230
Whoa, Inspector.

852
00:55:54,470 --> 00:55:55,770
That's a huge mosquito.

853
00:55:56,620 --> 00:55:57,900
It's feasting on your blood.

854
00:56:00,850 --> 00:56:02,040
Seriously?

855
00:56:02,280 --> 00:56:03,950
I thought you were going to kiss me.

856
00:56:04,420 --> 00:56:06,020
You had me going there for a second.

857
00:56:09,550 --> 00:56:11,380
You're pretty easy to read, too.

858
00:56:13,150 --> 00:56:14,380
Come on, let's get some sleep

859
00:56:15,250 --> 00:56:16,200
before the mosquitoes suck you dry.

860
00:56:35,200 --> 00:56:35,920
Hey.

861
00:56:37,310 --> 00:56:39,550
Can I sleep shirtless?
I'm basically a human furnace.

862
00:56:39,980 --> 00:56:40,780
No, you can't.

863
00:56:41,180 --> 00:56:43,320
What if my mom saw you like that
in the morning?

864
00:56:49,220 --> 00:56:50,150
Come on.

865
00:57:01,490 --> 00:57:02,170
Mungkorn...

866
00:57:04,960 --> 00:57:06,320
There's something
I really like about you.

867
00:57:08,660 --> 00:57:09,670
What is it?

868
00:57:12,450 --> 00:57:14,290
Honestly, it's quite a few things,

869
00:57:14,390 --> 00:57:16,260
but there's one thing in particular
that I really like.

870
00:57:17,610 --> 00:57:19,540
It's that you're never ashamed
to be yourself.

871
00:57:23,050 --> 00:57:24,470
You like teddy bears.

872
00:57:25,060 --> 00:57:26,590
You like bear-print pajamas.

873
00:57:26,940 --> 00:57:28,090
You love all things cute.

874
00:57:28,860 --> 00:57:31,480
To others, it might clash
with being a cop,

875
00:57:33,090 --> 00:57:34,300
but you don't care.

876
00:57:34,840 --> 00:57:36,510
I find it quite charming, actually.

877
00:57:37,000 --> 00:57:38,770
There's nothing to be ashamed of.

878
00:57:39,550 --> 00:57:43,090
Cuteness and strength
can definitely coexist.

879
00:57:43,350 --> 00:57:44,450
Just like with you.

880
00:58:01,590 --> 00:58:02,620
Right, Mungkorn.

881
00:58:03,550 --> 00:58:05,200
Can I ask one thing of you?

882
00:58:06,120 --> 00:58:08,700
If you're asking to cuddle my bear,
the answer is no.

883
00:58:09,090 --> 00:58:09,830
That's not it.

884
00:58:11,450 --> 00:58:13,060
Can you please call me...

885
00:58:13,590 --> 00:58:15,490
Thear the way your mom calls me?

886
00:58:15,530 --> 00:58:16,290
I really like it.

887
00:58:19,590 --> 00:58:21,850
Is that really a good idea?

888
00:58:23,060 --> 00:58:24,220
Of course it is.

889
00:58:25,160 --> 00:58:27,680
I think it sounds quite sweet.

890
00:58:44,350 --> 00:58:45,300
Goodnight,

891
00:58:46,910 --> 00:58:47,930
Thear.

892
00:58:50,240 --> 00:58:51,220
Goodnight,

893
00:58:51,670 --> 00:58:52,550
Mungkorn.

894
00:59:19,130 --> 00:59:23,930
♪I have a heart to give,
when will it be received?♪

895
00:59:25,150 --> 00:59:30,290
♪Can you hear it?
My love, can you hear my wishes?♪

896
00:59:30,950 --> 00:59:36,710
♪All of my heart, I've kept it all for you,♪

897
00:59:37,260 --> 00:59:42,360
♪And all I want is for it to belong to you♪

898
00:59:45,710 --> 00:59:50,800
♪If you ask how much I love you,
I'll let you know♪

899
00:59:51,510 --> 00:59:56,360
♪If you ask how much I care,
I'll tell you so♪

900
00:59:57,530 --> 01:00:02,040
♪I love you to the moon and back♪

901
01:00:03,370 --> 01:00:08,080
♪That's how much love I have packed♪

902
01:00:09,280 --> 01:00:14,520
♪About four hundred thousand miles,
or even more than that♪

903
01:00:17,320 --> 01:00:19,230
Do you have a ring
on your ring finger?

904
01:00:19,260 --> 01:00:20,610
Are you married,
or did you just put it there?

905
01:00:20,660 --> 01:00:21,850
Do you want to play a match with me?

906
01:00:21,890 --> 01:00:23,710
If you can't play well, I can teach you.

907
01:00:23,750 --> 01:00:25,590
I can tell at a glance

908
01:00:25,610 --> 01:00:27,870
he's got his sights set on you.

909
01:00:27,900 --> 01:00:29,130
What kind of sights?

910
01:00:30,280 --> 01:00:31,300
Don't you like it?

911
01:00:31,510 --> 01:00:33,620
We were only faking it last time.

912
01:00:33,640 --> 01:00:34,970
Let's make it real this time.

913
01:00:35,060 --> 01:00:35,800
Hey.

914
01:00:35,820 --> 01:00:37,900
Seductive like this...
Don't you like it?

915
01:00:37,930 --> 01:00:38,930
But...

916
01:00:38,970 --> 01:00:40,070
I'm here to serve you.

917
01:00:41,570 --> 01:00:46,480
♪Trying so hard not to cross the line,♪

918
01:00:46,510 --> 01:00:51,340
♪But the more I run,
the more you're on my mind♪

919
01:00:51,370 --> 01:00:55,640
♪If you're gonna love me,
don't break the deal we made♪

920
01:00:55,670 --> 01:01:01,190
♪Don't break my heart,
remember what you said?♪

921
01:01:01,220 --> 01:01:06,090
♪Let's call off the deal
and let our hearts decide♪

922
01:01:06,120 --> 01:01:12,550
♪From contracting parties to lovers,
does that sound alright?♪

923
01:01:18,750 --> 01:01:22,580
♪It's time you became mine♪
